<!--
  Aura Hi-Res launcher icon - "Muestreo" (Sampling), monochrome layer for the
  Android 13+ themed icons. Shape only: no colour, no gradient, no soft alpha.

  The arc is deliberately DROPPED here. A 50%-alpha hairline disappears once the
  system flattens the layer to a single tint and only muddies the mark; the seven
  samples alone still read as sampling, so they carry the icon.

  Dot radius is 3.45, NOT the heavier weight the colour layer could afford. The
  curve is flat at its tails, so the two outermost samples on each side sit only
  8.93 apart; at radius 3.8+ they fused into a single dash at 36, 40, 56 and 72px
  and the icon stopped being countable. 3.45 keeps all seven separate from 44px
  up while staying within ~2% of the colour layer's mass.

  This is a single FILLED path with no strokes - which is exactly what the old
  vinyl monochrome got wrong: its grooves were strokes, so the themed icon
  collapsed into a plain black dot.

  Furthest painted pixel from (54,54): 32.52, inside the r=33 safe circle.
-->
